[91.905802, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         The callback validates the returned state, exchanges the code for tokens\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         and user identity at the IdP token endpoint, and stores the user in the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         Flask session so protected portal routes recognise the request as\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         authenticated.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         \"\"\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         error = request.args.get(\"error\")\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>         if error:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>             return jsonify({\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>                 \"error\": error,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
